==================== MULTI-TASK ADMET PROJECTS ====================

1. MTAN-ADMET
Paper:
https://chemrxiv.org/doi/10.26434/chemrxiv-2025-zhrsk
GitHub:
https://github.com/TeamSuman/MTAN-ADMET
Dataset:
Zintegrowany ADMET dataset (Du et al., różne źródła publiczne)
~20–24 endpointów (BBB, CYP, hERG, solubility, toxicity itd.)
Opis:
SMILES → CDDD embeddings → MLP multitask
Mix: classification + regression
Brak graphów, gotowe preprocessing + split

------------------------------------------------------------

2. ADMET-AI
Paper:
https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11226862/
GitHub:
https://github.com/swansonk14/admet_ai
Dataset:
TDC (Therapeutics Data Commons)
41 datasetów:
- ~31 classification (toxicity, inhibition, BBB)
- ~10 regression (solubility, clearance itd.)
Opis:
SMILES → graph → D-MPNN (Chemprop)
Duży multitask model (40+ endpointów)

------------------------------------------------------------

3. MTGL-ADMET
Paper:
https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10654589/
GitHub:
https://github.com/dubingxue/MTGL-ADMET
Dataset:
MoleculeNet + public ADMET datasets
~10–15 endpointów (toxicity, physchem, metabolism)
Opis:
Graph neural network + task gating
Dynamiczne wybieranie auxiliary tasków

------------------------------------------------------------

4. Multitask GCN (MDPI)
Paper:
https://www.mdpi.com/1420-3049/25/1/44
GitHub:
brak
Dataset:
Physicochemical datasets (logP, solubility, permeability itd.)
~7–10 endpointów (regression)
Opis:
SMILES → graph → GCN → multitask regression
Bardzo prosty model (2–3 warstwy)

------------------------------------------------------------

5. MTAN (base architecture)
Paper:
https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.10704
GitHub:
https://github.com/lorenmt/mtan
Dataset:
Ogólne (np. vision: NYU v2, CityScapes)
(brak ADMET bezpośrednio)
Opis:
Shared backbone + task-specific attention
Można przenieść na ADMET

------------------------------------------------------------

6. Multi-task ADMET (Quantum + MTL)
Paper:
https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.04601
GitHub:
brak
Dataset:
TDC + quantum chemistry datasets
~13 endpointów ADMET
Opis:
SMILES + QM descriptors → multitask model
Wyższa dokładność, wysoka złożoność

------------------------------------------------------------

==================== PODSUMOWANIE ====================

MTAN-ADMET:
~20–24 tasks → najłatwiejszy start

ADMET-AI:
~40+ tasks → największy benchmark

MTGL-ADMET:
~10–15 tasks → inteligentny multitask

GCN (MDPI):
~7–10 tasks → najprostszy GNN

Quantum:
~13 tasks → najbardziej zaawansowany

